{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And the land shall not vomit you out, etc., as it vomited out, etc.</b> It was not enough that He said above ״and the land vomited out,״ to admonish more intensely — after the manner of what R. Eliezer ben Azariah expounded in the portion of Acharei Mot (Torat Kohanim, Acharei Mot, parashah 9): A parable of a sick man into whose presence the physician entered, etc. — Do not eat cold things, etc., lest you die in the manner that so-and-so died — this admonishes him more intensely, etc. — end quote. So too in our passage, HaShem intended to admonish Israel more intensely."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:58:37.286408339Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}